5. Finite onboarding propagation retry and side-effect-free auth reads.
6. Close Windows git repository handles before recovery and preserve measured TTFT semantics.
7. Translate ZCode base64 audio/video blocks to Gemini inlineData without weakening config-write guards.
8. Publish thinking levels and map ZCode Low/Medium/High to Gemini thinkingLevel.
9. Expose clean Gemini 3.7/3.6 Flash client IDs while routing to the exact upstream High entries.
10. Provide a SHA-256 verified installer with automatic Windows/v2rayN loopback proxy discovery, direct fallback, and no TUN requirement.
11. Stage and verify the payload, safely stop the recorded gateway, then deploy so same-version reruns cannot overwrite a running backend.
12. Add a no-console native control center that injects the Provider, manages the local bridge, and renders provider quota.
13. Apply system typography, responsive CSS controls, progress feedback, and crisp mixed-DPI rendering.
14. Encode the native installer's embedded Chinese PowerShell script with a UTF-8 BOM at build time and runtime for Windows PowerShell 5.1.
15. Start the Go Core and all PowerShell, tasklist, netstat, taskkill, OAuth, browser, and ZCode child processes without console windows.
16. Use an Electron + React/Tailwind main window with Segoe UI Variable, Chromium DPI scaling, and responsive relayout.
17. Add a persistent native Windows taskbar quota widget with provider switching and an explicit full-window action.
18. Add official xAI device OAuth, Grok text-model selection, Grok Build billing display, and encrypted-token-safe management proxying.
19. Add backed-up one-click setup for DeepSeek Harness, Grok Build, Codex, Claude Code, Gemini CLI, Qwen Code, Kimi Code, and OpenCode.
20. Retry Antigravity quota requests without project metadata after HTTP 403 and fall back to per-model quota data.
21. Collect sanitized backend usage records and expose provider-specific output Token, reasoning Token, and token/s metrics.
22. Show five-hour/week reset details and recent token performance in an independent taskbar-click widget without raising the main window.
23. Keep Antigravity/Grok quota caches isolated and reject stale provider-switch display updates.
24. Add a dedicated Gemini Web Search client model backed by Antigravity native Google Search, with grounded result blocks and citations.
24. Keep provider-specific Token caches isolated so Grok never displays Gemini usage while switching.
25. Preserve the real historical backend path when reusing a gateway and safely recover same-root legacy state during upgrades.
26. Honor --auto-setup in the native control center so a successful installer launch begins bridge setup automatically.
27. Use native DWM Acrylic without desktop capture and pause ambient CSS animation during native move/resize.
28. Refuse release builds without working Antigravity OAuth desktop configuration and automatically recover a recorded bridge after an unexpected process exit.
29. Treat a provider with no logged-in account as a normal empty quota state instead of HTTP 503, and isolate quota refresh failures from dashboard status.
30. Lower the native Acrylic tint and frontend glass-layer opacity so the live desktop blur remains visible behind readable controls.
31. Separate tray-click and main-window activation, add a DPI-aware always-on-top quota popup, and strengthen specular Acrylic layers.
32. Match the macOS light liquid-glass information architecture and remove nested blur layers from scrollable content.
33. Replace the Rust/Tauri shell with Electron 44 while preserving the tested Go native-host API and React theme.
34. Enable context isolation and renderer sandboxing, disable Node integration, and expose only fixed IPC methods.
35. Use DWM Acrylic for the main window and independent tray widget while removing renderer-side full-window blur during scroll and drag.
36. Restrict liquid glass to the white window backdrop; keep navigation, cards, buttons, and text on high-contrast surfaces, with zero renderer animations in Electron mode.

